# Repository Test Doubles

Entity tests replace `IBlingRepository` with a PHPUnit mock. They assert the `RequestOptions` the entity built and the object returned by `fromResponse`.

## Setup

From `src/Entities/Contatos/__tests__/ContatosTest.spec.php`:

```php
$repository = $this->getMockBuilder(IBlingRepository::class)->getMock();
$entity = new Contatos($repository);
```

Construct the entity with the mock. Do not construct `Bling` inside an entity spec. Facade coverage lives in `src/BlingTest.spec.php`.

Before the call, annotate the mock as `/** @var \AleBatistella\BlingErpApi\Repositories\IBlingRepository&\PHPUnit\Framework\MockObject\MockObject $repository */`.

The spec class `use`s `AleBatistella\BlingErpApi\Entities\Shared\TestResponseTrait`.

## Response helper

`TestResponseTrait::buildResponse` returns a `ResponseOptions`:

| Parameter | Role |
|-----------|------|
| `$endpoint` | Defaults to `fake()->word()` |
| `$method` | Defaults to `fake()->word()` |
| `$status` | Defaults to a number from 200 to 500. Success tests pass `status: 200` |
| `$headers` | `Headers` or `null`. Build with `buildHeaders(array)` |
| `$body` | `Body` or `null`. Build with `buildBody(array)` |

`buildBody(null)` and `buildHeaders(null)` return `null`.

## Expectation

```php
$repository->expects($this->once())
    ->method('show')
    ->with($this->callback(
        fn (RequestOptions $requestOptions) =>
            $requestOptions->endpoint === "contatos/$idContato"
    ))
    ->willReturn($this->buildResponse(status: 200, body: $this->buildBody($findResponse)));
```

The verb is the one the entity calls. The callback reads `endpoint`, and `queryParams->content` or `headers` when the call sets them.

## Ids

Generate numeric ids with `fake()->randomNumber()` and interpolate them into the expected endpoint. Keep fixture JSON ids stable; they are payload data, not the path id under test.

## Error specs

`ResponseOptionsTest` constructs `ResponseOptions` with status `400`. A body shaped as `ErrorResponse` expects `BlingApiException` and the `error.description` message. A `400` body that is not that shape expects `BlingInternalException`. `ErrorResponseTest` covers `ErrorResponse::from` and the same exception path.

## Scope

These doubles do not perform HTTP. A new repository method is added to `IBlingRepository` first; specs then `method('<name>')` on the same `getMockBuilder(IBlingRepository::class)` mock.
